# Stack Best Practices

## TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled everywhere via `packages/typescript-config/base.json`: `strict: true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true`
- Target: `ES2022`, module: `NodeNext`, moduleResolution: `NodeNext`
- Always use `.js` extension in relative imports (even for `.ts` files): `import { FarmEngine } from "./engine.js"`
- Use `import.meta.url` with `fileURLToPath()` instead of `__dirname` / `__filename`
- Infer types from Zod schemas: `type WorkOrder = z.infer<typeof WorkOrderSchema>` — avoid duplicating types manually

## Zod
- Define all schemas in `@repo/shared` (`packages/shared/src/`): models in `models.ts`, events in `events.ts`, API contracts in `api.ts`, agent schemas in `agents.ts`
- Infer TypeScript types with `z.infer<typeof Schema>` — schemas are the single source of truth
- Parse at API boundaries with `.parse()`: `CreateWorkOrderRequest.parse(request.body)` in route handlers
- Use discriminated unions for polymorphic data: `FarmEventSchema` discriminates on `type` field
- Use `z.record(z.unknown())` for freeform JSON objects (e.g., `WorkOrder.context`)
- Use `.default()` for optional fields with defaults: `z.string().default("")`, `z.array(...).default([])`

## Fastify
- Register routes via exported functions: `registerApiRoutes(app, engine, adapter)`, `registerPublicRoutes(app, engine, adapter, prisma)`
- Use Zod `.parse()` on `request.body` / `request.query` — do not use Fastify's built-in JSON Schema validation
- Return proper HTTP status codes: `201` for creation, `405` for method-not-allowed on public routes
- Type route params with generics: `app.post<{ Params: { id: string } }>("/api/tasks/:id/assign", ...)`

## Prisma + SQLite
- JSON fields are stored as `String` columns: `context`, `deps`, `payload`
- Serialize with `JSON.stringify()` when writing; deserialize with `JSON.parse()` in `PrismaAdapter` helper methods (`toWorkOrder()`, `toTask()`, `toArtifact()`, `toDecision()`, `toEventLog()`)
- Date fields are `DateTime` in Prisma, converted to ISO strings via `.toISOString()` in adapter helpers
- Use `@default(uuid())` for primary keys, `@updatedAt` for automatic update timestamps
- Define indexes on frequently queried columns: `@@index([workOrderId])`, `@@index([status])`, `@@index([timestamp])`

## React Components
- All `@repo/ui` components (`packages/ui/src/*.tsx`) must start with `"use client"` directive
- Use `cva` from `class-variance-authority` for variant-based styling (see `packages/ui/src/button.tsx`)
- Use `cn()` from `@repo/ui/lib/utils` (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) for className merging
- Define component props as inline object types: `function Button({ className, variant, size, ...props }: ButtonPrimitive.Props & VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants>)`
- Use `@base-ui/react` primitives only inside `@repo/ui` — app code imports from `@repo/ui/*`

## Tailwind CSS v4
- CSS-first configuration — no `tailwind.config.js` / `tailwind.config.ts`
- Use `@theme` directive in CSS for design tokens
- Use `tailwind-merge` (via `cn()`) to safely merge conditional classes

## Testing (Vitest)
- Test files live alongside source or in `__tests__/` directories, named `*.test.ts`
- Standard `beforeEach` setup for engine tests:
  ```
  registerAllRoles()
  eventBus = new EventBus()
  adapter = new InMemoryAdapter()
  engine = new FarmEngine(adapter, eventBus)
  emittedEvents = []
  eventBus.onAny((event) => emittedEvents.push(event))
  ```
- Use `InMemoryAdapter` from `packages/core/src/testing/in-memory-adapter.ts` — never depend on SQLite in unit tests
- Assert events by filtering `emittedEvents.map(e => e.type)`
- Test invalid transitions with `expect(...).rejects.toThrow("Invalid status transition")`

## Imports & Dependencies
- Internal packages use `workspace:*` protocol in `package.json`
- Use subpath imports for `@repo/shared`, `@repo/core`, `@repo/memory`: `import { StatusEnum } from "@repo/shared/statuses"`
- Use wildcard imports for `@repo/ui`: `import { Button } from "@repo/ui/button"`
- Use `@repo/ui/lib/utils` for the `cn()` utility

## ESM
- All packages are `"type": "module"` — no CommonJS anywhere
- Use `import` / `export` exclusively
- Use `import.meta.url` for path resolution: `const __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)`
- ESLint uses flat config format: all `eslint.config.mjs` files import `config` from `@repo/eslint-config/base.js`
- `eslint-plugin-only-warn` is enabled globally — ESLint errors are treated as warnings
